{"id": "EUVD-2026-90648", "enisaUuid": "f74ad821-65e9-3177-891c-636c45c2a43f", "description": "n8n versions before 1.123.80, from 2.0.0 before 2.39.6, and from 2.40.0 before 2.40.1 contain a path traversal vulnerability in signed resume URL generation for Send-and-Wait approvals. Attackers with workflow creation permissions can mint valid approval URLs for gates in projects they cannot access by exploiting unresolved traversal sequences in caller-controlled node IDs, enabling cross-project approval forgery.", "datePublished": "2026-10-01T10:41:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-06T00:06:56", "baseScore": 7.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:H/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/security/advisories/GHSA-597w-c3jh-g8fg", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/n8n-before-1.123.80-2.39.6-and-2.40.1-path-traversal-via-resume-url-generation"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-103254", "GHSA-w2h3-gf8c-fwgw"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2f8a72f3-b92e-3add-819a-cf9fee38928c", "product": {"name": "n8n", "vendor": {"name": "n8n-io"}}, "product_version": "2.40.0 <2.40.1"}, {"id": "816fc8d7-10ec-3744-872a-a185fc8a6ab7", "product": {"name": "n8n", "vendor": {"name": "n8n-io"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.123.80"}, {"id": "aad15aa7-2889-36e4-bb65-95f39db61984", "product": {"name": "n8n", "vendor": {"name": "n8n-io"}}, "product_version": "2.0.0 <2.39.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6d8b2ba2-fbc1-370d-a126-32d56e581938", "vendor": {"name": "n8n-io"}}], "isExploited": false}